Depends: ohpc-filesystem, intel-compilers-devel-ohpc, mvapich2-intel-ohpc, hypre-intel-mvapich2-ohpc, metis-intel-ohpc, netcdf-intel-mvapich2-ohpc, petsc-intel-mvapich2-ohpc (>= 3.12.0), ptscotch-intel-mvapich2-ohpc, superlu-dist-intel-mvapich2-ohpc, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Lightweight, general, scalable C++ library for finite element methods (intel + mvapich2, OpenHPC)
 MFEM is a modular parallel C++ library for finite element methods. Its goal is
 to enable the research and development of scalable finite element discretization
 and solver algorithms through general finite element abstractions, accurate and
 flexible visualization, and tight integration with the hypre library.
 Built with the intel compiler family and mvapich2 MPI stack.
 .
 This package is part of the OpenHPC project.
